    {
      "id": "0f0d9b38-d11c-4767-b5e5-1cf40cdad152",
      "name": "Sticky Note 8c29e4eb",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -60,
        20
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Job Scout: daily scan\n\nEvery morning this path scans the Ashby boards listed in **Job Scout config**, saves one lead per posting in the `leads` Data Table, and sends the newest unsent leads to Telegram.\n\n**Setup**\n1. Create a bot with @BotFather and pick its credential on **Send header** and **Send lead message**.\n2. Fill in **Job Scout config** (see the note below it).\n3. Publish the workflow.\n\nThe `leads` table is created on the first run if it doesn't exist. Job Scout never applies for jobs or contacts anyone.",
        "color": 4,
        "width": 460,
        "height": 320
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "8ccd1650-86b4-4d96-8331-7016e70ba153",
      "name": "Sticky Note 7145acf8",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -60,
        580
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Job Scout config\n\nEdit these fields in the **Job Scout config** node:\n\n- **ashbyBoards**: Ashby board names to scan, as a list. The board name is the part after `jobs.ashbyhq.com/` in a company's job board link. Default: `n8n`, `posthog`, `ramp`.\n- **telegramChatId**: the chat the daily ping goes to. Tap Start in your bot, open `https://api.telegram.org/bot<token>/getUpdates` once, and copy `message.chat.id`.\n- **dailyCap**: the most leads one daily ping sends. Leads over the cap stay New and go out on a later day. Default 10.\n- **tablePrefix**: put in front of every Data Table name, so `jobscout_` gives `jobscout_leads`. n8n looks tables up by a \"name contains\" match, so no other table name may contain the full name (for example, don't use an empty prefix if `jobscout_leads` exists). The tests use `jobscout_test_`.\n\n**Run time** is set on the **Daily scan** trigger, not here, because a trigger's settings can't read other nodes. Default 8:00 in the instance timezone. If n8n is down at that time, the most recent missed scan runs when it comes back.",
        "color": 6,
        "width": 700,
        "height": 440
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "9f930857-7eaa-4eee-bab6-39cd045e320d",
      "name": "Sticky Note 3d1fc0d5",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        1480,
        580
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Save leads\n\nA lead is keyed by `ashby:<board>:<job id>`.\n\n- **Save lead** upserts on that key, so a second scan updates the posting fields and `last_seen_at` instead of adding a row.\n- **Mark first sighting** gives rows with no status yet `status = new` and `first_seen_at = now`. Rows that already have a status keep their first-seen date.",
        "color": 7,
        "width": 420,
        "height": 260
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "f25660e2-4c47-4069-b2df-cad6bcdd9c4f",
      "name": "Sticky Note c14e9032",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        2160,
        640
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Daily ping\n\n- **Get leads to send** picks leads with status `new` and no `sent_at`, newest posting first, up to `dailyCap`. If there are none, nothing is sent.\n- **Send header** sends \"Job Scout: N new leads today\" with sound.\n- Each lead goes out as its own silent message with an **Open posting** button, one per second.\n- **Mark sent** sets `sent_at` right after each message, so no lead is sent twice.\n\nBoth Telegram nodes use HTML parse mode and have the n8n attribution line turned off.",
        "color": 5,
        "width": 560,
        "height": 300
      }
    }
  ],
